<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The werust app theme, LIGHT variant (task webview-follow-os-color-scheme,
  docs/adr/0009).

  WHY A THEME PER LIGHT/NIGHT: Android's System WebView ALWAYS sets the page's
  `prefers-color-scheme` from the app theme's `isLightTheme` attribute (Android
  developer docs, "Darken web content in WebView"): isLightTheme=true (or unset)
  reports `prefers-color-scheme: light`, else `dark`. The app previously used the
  fixed LIGHT framework theme (@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar),
  so the WebView reported LIGHT even in OS dark mode, mismatching the user's
  setting and theming UA controls light on a dark page (the mandalas.eth.limo
  white-on-white buttons).

  THE FIX = FOLLOW the OS, never force: this LIGHT variant (values/) has
  isLightTheme=true; the NIGHT variant (values-night/themes.xml) has
  isLightTheme=false. Android selects the variant by the OS night-mode qualifier
  (UI_MODE_NIGHT), so the WebView's `prefers-color-scheme` follows the OS
  light/dark setting. It does NOT force dark and does NOT enable algorithmic
  darkening, so a page's own declared `color-scheme` is still respected: we only
  supply the OS preference as the default the page and UA styling resolve against.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.Werust" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:isLightTheme">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
